    "Toshio": "Focused on minimizing the administrative burden. He argues against any system that requires constant chasing of small sums.",
    "Jonathan": "Cares about the psychological barrier to attendance. He opposes any structure that makes members weigh the cost of coming out.",
    "Takumi": "Concerned with fairness and the imbalance of contribution. He initially seeks a way to differentiate between heavy and light users.",
    "Kenji": "Values inclusivity and low barriers to entry. He worries about social hierarchies and the deterrent effect of high upfront costs."
  },
